From: OrangeFox PECM30 device maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] keystore2: use binderized HIDL manager in recovery

Recovery builds normally force generated HIDL getService() calls through the
passthrough transport. PECM30 recovery runs a binderized hwservicemanager, so
the built-in KeyMint compatibility layer must obtain that manager directly.

diff --git a/keystore2/src/km_compat/km_compat.cpp b/keystore2/src/km_compat/km_compat.cpp
index 2823c24..bc4aad7 100644
--- a/keystore2/src/km_compat/km_compat.cpp
+++ b/keystore2/src/km_compat/km_compat.cpp
@@ -27,0 +28 @@
+#include <hidl/ServiceManagement.h>
@@ -1314 +1315 @@ KeymasterDevices initializeKeymasters() {
-    auto serviceManager = IServiceManager::getService();
+    auto serviceManager = android::hardware::defaultServiceManager1_2();
